#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:539
msgid ""
"``TCC_REQ[n]`` may be more than the number of requests arriving at the "
"texture cache per channel, but it's a good indication of the total amount"
" of work that needs to be performed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:541
msgid ""
"For ``TCC_EA0_WRREQ[n]``, atomics may travel over the same interface and "
"are generally classified as write requests."
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:543
msgid ""
"CC mtypes can produce uncached requests, and those are included in "
"``TCC_EA0_WR_UNCACHED_32B[n]``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:545
msgid ""
"``TCC_EA0_WRREQ_LEVEL[n]`` is primarily intended to measure average "
"efficiency arbiter write latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:547
msgid ""
"Average write latency = ``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_WRREQ_LEVEL`` divided by "
"``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_WRREQ``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:549
msgid ""
"``TCC_EA0_ATOMIC_LEVEL[n]`` is primarily intended to measure average "
"efficiency arbiter atomic latency"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:552
msgid ""
"Average atomic latency = ``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_WRREQ_ATOMIC_LEVEL`` divided "
"by ``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_WRREQ_ATOMIC``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:554
msgid ""
"``TCC_EA0_RDREQ_LEVEL[n]`` is primarily intended to measure average "
"efficiency arbiter read latency."
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:556
msgid ""
"Average read latency = ``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_RDREQ_LEVEL`` divided by "
"``TCC_PERF_SEL_EA0_RDREQ``"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:558
msgid "Stalls can occur regardless of the need for a read to be performed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../conceptual/gpu-arch/mi300-mi200-performance-counters.rst:559
msgid ""
"Normally, stalls are measured exactly at one point in the pipeline "
"however in the case of ``TCC_TAG_STALL[n]``, probes can stall the "
"pipeline at a variety of places. There is no single point that can "
"accurately measure the total stalls"
msgstr ""

